Nice to know you had some time to look at this issue I'm experiencing.

Ok you are right :) in each tabsetPanel its ok, 2 tabs/panes. Sorry for the poor English.

What is not ok is the number of tabsetPanels spreading across the columns.

Each group has 12 values, when the user selects one of them the expected behavior is to show  6 rows, each one with 2 "cells", each one with a tabsetPanel with 2 panes.

It works as intended under some circunstances, but some note as I cited, it doesnt.

It shows just one row with 2 "cells" each one with a tabsetPanel with 2 panes. As I tried to track the error it seems the tabsetPanels are being created, maybe being overwriteen or superimposed by the new ones.

Regards

João Carlos

