Date: Tue, 15 Nov 2016 20:19:07 +0000
Subject: Re: Detecting a mobile user
Message-ID: <yAO0QV1uWDc.ud09L1c5BQAJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/yAO0QV1uWDc/m/ud09L1c5BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For anyone who is interested:

We are using the following JS to detect mobile:

function isMobile(){
try{document.createEvent('TouchEvent'); return true;}
catch(e){return false;}
}

I know that isn’t fool-proof, but it serves the purpose.

With that, we are then assigning a Shiny input binding either 0 or 1 based off of the isMobile() data.

Works like a charm.

~ Laz Peterson
Paravis, LLC

> On Nov 14, 2016, at 7:10 AM, Laz C. Peterson <l...@paravis.net> wrote:
>
> Hello all —
>
> Does anyone have any recommendations about detecting a mobile-sized screen in the server code and preparing data differently for that type of device?
>
> We use Mobile Detect for our other websites (http://mobiledetect.net/) but that’s written in PHP and obviously won’t work for Shiny.
>
> ~ Laz Peterson
> Paravis, LLC
